/-!
# Certified surviving generator images for J₁

For each of the 1463 literal involution matrices, the certificate either rejects
one of the two required relators or constructs a word in the actual matrix model
which centralizes `b` and conjugates `a` to that row. Rejections are certified by
short vector trajectories; the 30 conjugators are checked using the proved
matrix images of the order-certificate words and two intertwining identities.
The arithmetic block cover below exhausts every index, independently of the
untrusted search counts. No orbit-closure assumption is used.

This proves the generator-image part of the calculation supporting GLS3,
Table 5.3f. See `Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko1.Model.Basic` for the ATLAS matrices
and relators, and `Source/` for the untrusted searches. `GeneratorImages/Generate.py`
regenerates the finite proofs, all of which are checked by the Lean kernel.
-/

namespace Janko1.OuterCertificate

/-- Every admissible generator image is realized by an element centralizing `b`. -/
